            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0248" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1084: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-01T16:00:00-04:00">February 1, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. My telegram No. 19, January 31, 7 p.m., and Department’s instruction No. 1449
                    air mail January 15th [<hi rendition="#italic">19th</hi>].<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d141-f1"/> Proposed law will result in advantage to certain British
                    interests. Conversations with members of British Embassy and with American
                    nitrate representative indicate that we cannot count on British diplomacy in
                    this issue. On other issues this may not be the case but there is no indication
                    that Ross’ program is meeting with British opposition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d141-f1" n="50" xml:id="d141-f1-content">
                <p>Instruction No. 1449 not printed.</p>
            </note>
